<title>PERU: Peru's August cotton output rises 102 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's August cotton output rises 102 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's August cotton production rose 102 percent to 57,930 tonnes from the same month last year, Agriculture Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Output in the first eight months rose 24 percent to 225,269 tonnes from the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 216,869 tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports of uncombed cotton in August fell 83 percent to 1,031 tonnes, worth $1.132 million, while imports in the first eight months dropped 58 percent to 11,690 tonnes, worth $12.651 million.</p>
<p>August cotton exports rose 206 percent to 940 tonnes, worth $2.380 million, while exports in the first eight months increased 181 percent to 6,747 tonnes, worth $19.201 million.</p>
<p>--Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
